xnu 0276: publish one touch position for each display tick

The panel follows the events: a drag redraws once per position it is handed, so
the spacing of the events is the spacing of the motion. The report thread wakes
on its own `tsleep()` timeout about twice a frame and used to hand the UI a
position on every wake -- measured, ring243: 85-120 events a second with `ev gap
avg 11.7 ms` and 27 of the intervals under 10 ms, i.e. a step, a half step, a
step. No frame rate fixes that: the content itself advances unevenly.

`mondrian_touch_vsync()` now counts the display ticks, and the thread publishes
the newest position once per tick and never in between. Reading is unchanged --
every wake still drains the part (360 reports a second measured), so the
position published at a tick is the freshest one, and a finger that lifts
between ticks is still reported up at the next one.

